{"id":"aufgelo_st","lemma":"aufgelöst","pos":"adj","rank":3822,"glosses":["dissolved, drained","distraught, exhausted, upset"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c1/De-aufgel%C3%B6st.ogg/De-aufgel%C3%B6st.ogg.mp3","forms":{"comparative":"aufgelöster","superlative":"am aufgelöstesten"},"examples":[{"text":"Ich habe unsere Verlobung aufgelöst.","en":"I've broken off our engagement.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"have","l":"haben"},{"g":"our","l":"unser"},{"g":"engagement, betrothal"},null]},{"text":"Tom war in Tränen aufgelöst.","en":"Tom was in tears.","words":[null,{"g":"was","l":"sein"},{"g":"in"},{"g":"to water"},null]},{"text":"Mein Fahrrad hat sich in Luft aufgelöst.","en":"My bike vanished into thin air.","words":[{"g":"my"},{"g":"bicycle"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"oneself"},{"g":"in"},{"g":"air, atmosphere"},null]},{"text":"Es ist wahrscheinlich, dass das Parlament aufgelöst wird.","en":"It's likely the Diet will be dissolved.","words":[{"g":"it"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"probably, likely"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"parliament"},null,{"g":"to become","l":"werden"}]},{"text":"Der Junge sagte, das Taxi habe sich im Nebel aufgelöst.","en":"The boy said that the taxi vanished into the fog.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"boy"},{"g":"to say (to pronounce","l":"sagen"},{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"taxi, cab"},{"g":"have","l":"haben"},{"g":"oneself"},{"g":"in the"},{"g":"fog, mist, haze"},null]}]}